                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7971a493-657c-344f-a31d-49071229e32a",
                        "entry_id": "f18c2310-eda6-3e9b-ad9f-69628e504c40",
                        "glosses": [
                            "английское женское имя"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7eb9e6fc-009b-482d-8b59-7a5083d0c5dd",
                                "sense_id": "7971a493-657c-344f-a31d-49071229e32a",
                                "text": "И так получилось, что его аспирантка Элейн Гриффитс неоконченного «Хоббита» читала."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5150c39d-c592-492c-8f5c-5979201f131f",
                                "sense_id": "7971a493-657c-344f-a31d-49071229e32a",
                                "text": "По датам получается, что популярность песни из фильма не могла повлиять на тексты в антологии. На английский стихотворение перевела Элейн Файнстайн. Перевод без рифмы, он основан на ритме и отлично передает пульс ахмадулинской строки."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe9f87a8-fd70-429e-b78d-b9e11a6c0786",
                        "source_entry_id": "f18c2310-eda6-3e9b-ad9f-69628e504c40",
                        "source_sense_id": "7971a493-657c-344f-a31d-49071229e32a",
                        "target_lang_word": "Elaine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Elaine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a43efec-e1c9-3e3a-a62c-7b532bccd464",
                                        "entry_id": "283300e2-a80f-33f6-a52f-d751c50d0ccf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female given name from Ancient Greek."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9eefe0b3-a1d0-4dfb-bebc-41a7e4bb4a90",
                                                "sense_id": "3a43efec-e1c9-3e3a-a62c-7b532bccd464",
                                                "text": "Elaine the fair, Elaine the lovable,\nElaine, the lily maid of Astolat,\nHigh in her chamber up a tower to the east\nGuarded the sacred shield of Lancelot;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a36d9eca-6879-4b6d-a608-a8a5f7f4d313",
                                                "sense_id": "3a43efec-e1c9-3e3a-a62c-7b532bccd464",
                                                "text": "My own mother named me after her best friend, as women did in those days. Elaine, which I once found too plaintive. I wanted something more definite, a monosyllable: Dot or Pat, like a foot set down. Nothing you could make a mistake about; nothing watery. But my name has solidified around me, with time. I think of it as tough but pliable now, like a well-worn glove."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
